11. Use CSS @property

This is a relatively modern CSS capability that can produce very nice effects.

For example:

@property --angle {
  syntax: "<angle>";
  initial-value: 0deg;
  inherits: false;
}

Then:

.security-ring {
  background:
    conic-gradient(
      from var(--angle),
      transparent,
      #53d7d1,
      transparent
    );
  animation: rotate 6s linear infinite;
}

You can use that for:

progress rings
scanner indicators
active lab status
path progression
challenge state

It gives you sophisticated visuals without adding another dependency.

